100 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 57 0 R
/E (\(North, East, South and West\) controlled by traffic lights. It is a beginner-level Data Structures and Algorithms \(DSA\) project built with Java and Spring Boot for the backend and HTML, CSS and JavaScript for the frontend.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
101 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 57 0 R
/E (A Circular Linked List stores the signal phases of the junction, so that after the last direction the cycle automatically returns to the first one. A Queue stores the vehicles waiting at each road, and vehicles leave the queue in First-In-First-Out \(FIFO\) order when their signal turns green. A HashMap stores the green-light duration of every road. Java string operations are used to validate the road name entered by the user.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
102 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 57 0 R
/E (The browser asks a Spring Boot REST endpoint for the current state of the junction every second, and the page displays the signal colours, the remaining time and the number of waiting vehicles. The project uses simple predefined timings and does not need a database or any advanced features, which keeps the scope suitable for a college-level submission.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
